# Accepted trivy config findings, with reasons. Each entry is a ruling per
# the Unit 3.4 discipline: fixed, or accepted with the reason written down.
# Revisit when the architecture changes (a WAF, a KMS budget, a second AZ).

# AWS-0011 (HIGH): CloudFront distribution has no WAF.
# Accepted: static site and demo ingress, GET/HEAD only, no auth, no user
# data. A WAF's monthly cost exceeds the entire site's standing cost.
AVD-AWS-0011

# AWS-0132 (HIGH): S3 buckets use SSE-S3 (AES256) rather than a customer
# managed KMS key. Accepted: the buckets hold public site bytes and Terraform
# state in a single-admin account; CMK rotation and key policy management add
# cost and a lockout failure mode with no confidentiality gain here.
AVD-AWS-0132

# AWS-0104 (CRITICAL): recipe proxy security group allows egress to 0.0.0.0/0
# on 80/443/3478/41641. Accepted: Tailscale control plane, DERP relays, and
# package mirrors have no stable published CIDR set; each rule is
# port-scoped and documented in stacks/recipe/instance.tf.
AVD-AWS-0104

# AWS-0131 (HIGH): recipe proxy root volume is not encrypted. Accepted for
# now: t4g.nano ingress proxy holding no data at rest beyond the OS; fixing
# it forces instance replacement on a live demo. Candidate fix at the next
# instance rebuild: root_block_device { encrypted = true }.
AVD-AWS-0131

# AWS-0164 (HIGH): recipe public subnet auto-assigns public IPs. Accepted:
# the subnet exists to host the internet-facing ingress proxy; that is its
# job, and nothing else launches there.
AVD-AWS-0164
